        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages by GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, United States.</p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies and has no forms. Its pages, fonts and images are served from netria.dev itself.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> GitHub records technical details of each request, including your IP address, to run and secure the service. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Visit statistics.</strong> Each page loads Cloudflare Web Analytics from Cloudflare, Inc. (US). It receives your IP address, the page address, the page that linked to it, your browser type and page-load timings. It sets no cookies and doesn't follow you across sites; we only see totals. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Animation library.</strong> On desktop browsers that support WebGPU, the contact section loads an animation library from jsDelivr (cdn.jsdelivr.net), which receives your IP address. See the <a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net">jsDelivr privacy policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Email.</strong> If you write to {{ site.email }}, we use your address and message to reply and to work with you. Our email is hosted by Proton AG in Switzerland; see the <a href="https://proton.me/legal/privacy">Proton privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Under Moroccan law 09-08 on personal data, and the GDPR if you are in the European Union, you can ask what personal data we hold about you and have it corrected or deleted. Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

        <p>Last updated 20 October 2026.</p>
